  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Nephi",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "Lehi predicts that the Jews will be taken captive by the Babylonians—He tells of the coming among the Jews of a Messiah, a Savior, a Redeemer—Lehi tells also of the coming of the one who should baptize the Lamb of God—Lehi tells of the death and resurrection of the Messiah—He compares the scattering and gathering of Israel to an olive tree—Nephi speaks of the Son of God, of the gift of the Holy Ghost, and of the need for righteousness. About 600–592 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And now I, Nephi, proceed to give an account upon these plates of my proceedings, and my reign and ministry; wherefore, to proceed with mine account, I must speak somewhat of the things of my father, and also of my brethren.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "1 Ne. 9:2 (1–5); 19:3 (1–6)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Nephi 10:1",
        "book": "1 Nephi",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "For behold, it came to pass after my father had made an end of speaking the words of his dream, and also of exhorting them to all diligence, he spake unto them concerning the Jews—",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "1 Ne. 8:2 (2–36)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Nephi 10:2",
        "book": "1 Nephi",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "That after they should be destroyed, even that great city Jerusalem, and many be carried away captive into Babylon, according to the own due time of the Lord, they should return again, yea, even be brought back out of captivity; and after they should be brought back out of captivity they should possess again the land of their inheritance.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Esth. 2:6; 2 Ne. 6:8; Hel. 8:20 (20–21)."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "Ezek. 36:12 (8–15); 2 Ne. 25:10. TG Israel, Bondage of, in Other Lands; Israel, Scattering of."
          },
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 114,
            "text": "Ezek. 24:2; 1 Ne. 1:13; Omni 1:15. TG Babylon."
          },
          {
            "start": 171,
            "end": 177,
            "text": "Neh. 12:1; Jer. 29:10 (9–10); 2 Ne. 6:9 (8–9); Abr. 2:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Nephi 10:3",
        "book": "1 Nephi",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, even six hundred years from the time that my father left Jerusalem, a prophet would the Lord God raise up among the Jews—even a Messiah, or, in other words, a Savior of the world.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "1 Ne. 19:8 (8–14); 2 Ne. 25:19; Alma 13:25; 3 Ne. 1:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "1 Ne. 22:21 (20–21)."
          },
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "TG Israel, Judah, People of."
          },
          {
            "start": 133,
            "end": 140,
            "text": "Jacob 1:6. TG Jesus Christ, Birth of; Jesus Christ, Messiah."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
